{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And I, behold, I have given with him Oholiav son of Ahisamakh, of the tribe of Dan.</b> R. Chanina said: there is none greater than the tribe of Judah and none lowlier than the tribe of Dan, for he was of the lowly. The Holy One, blessed be He, said: let him be joined with him, so that his spirit not grow haughty — for great and small are equal before the Holy One, blessed be He. The Mishkan was made through both of them, this one from the tribe of Judah and this one from the tribe of Dan. And likewise the Temple was built through these two tribes: Shelomo from the tribe of Judah and Chiram from the tribe of Dan on his mother's side, as it is written in Chronicles (II Chronicles 2:13): ״בן אשה מן בנות דן״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:05:54.192413207Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}